@startuml Frontend vs Webhook Flow Comparison
!theme plain
title <font size=24 color="#1565C0"><b>THE AMBIGUITY: Frontend vs Webhook Flow</b></font>\n<font size=14 color="#1976D2">Same state machine, different implementations!</font>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000

left to right direction

rectangle "Frontend Flow\n<font color='#2E7D32'>(Contract-Aware - WORKS)</font>" as Frontend #C8E6C9 {
    rectangle "1. StripeContractCreationHandler" as F1 #A5D6A7
    rectangle "2. StripeCheckoutSessionHandler" as F2 #A5D6A7
    rectangle "3. StripeCheckoutReturnHandler" as F3 #A5D6A7
    rectangle "4. PaymentAuthorizedEventHandler" as F4 #A5D6A7
    rectangle "5. StripeOrderCreationHandler" as F5 #A5D6A7

    F1 --> F2
    F2 --> F3
    F3 --> F4
    F4 --> F5
}

rectangle "Contract State Machine" as Contract #FFF9C4 {
    rectangle "DRAFT" as Draft #2196F3
    rectangle "PENDING" as Pending #FF9800
    rectangle "READY_TO_COMMIT" as Ready #4CAF50
    rectangle "COMMITTED" as Committed #8BC34A
    rectangle "FULFILLED" as Fulfilled #009688

    Draft --> Pending
    Pending --> Ready
    Ready --> Committed
    Committed --> Fulfilled : <font color='#C62828'><b>MISSING!</b></font>
}

rectangle "Webhook Flow\n<font color='#C62828'>(Direct DB - BROKEN)</font>" as Webhook #FFCDD2 {
    rectangle "WebhookController" as W1 #EF9A9A
    rectangle "WebhookProcessingService" as W2 #EF9A9A
    rectangle "Direct SQL Updates" as W3 #EF9A9A

    W1 --> W2
    W2 --> W3
}

' Connections from Frontend to Contract
F1 ..> Draft : Creates
F4 ..> Pending : Transitions to
F4 ..> Ready : When conditions met
F5 ..> Committed : After order created

' Connection from Webhook (or lack thereof)
W2 ..> Committed : <font color='#C62828'>Ignores!</font>
W3 ..> Fulfilled : <font color='#C62828'>Doesn't transition!</font>

note right of Frontend
  <font color='#2E7D32'><b>Uses:</b></font>
  - ContractRepository
  - EventDispatcher
  - Contract state machine
  - PaymentContract model

  <b>State Transitions:</b>
  DRAFT -> PENDING -> READY -> COMMITTED
end note

note right of Webhook
  <font color='#C62828'><b>Bypasses:</b></font>
  - ContractRepository
  - EventDispatcher
  - Contract state machine
  - PaymentContract model

  <b>Direct SQL:</b>
  UPDATE osc_payment_order_state
  UPDATE oxorder (OXPAID, OXTRANSSTATUS)
end note

note bottom of Contract
  <font color='#E65100'><b>THE GAP:</b></font>
  Frontend reaches COMMITTED state correctly.
  Webhook should transition COMMITTED -> FULFILLED.
  But WebhookProcessingService doesn't touch contract!

  <b>Result:</b>
  Contract stuck in COMMITTED forever.
  Order marked paid via direct SQL.
  State machine broken.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Flow |= Uses Contract? |= Updates Via |= State Transitions |
  | <#C8E6C9> Frontend | YES | Repository + Events | DRAFT->PENDING->READY->COMMITTED |
  | <#FFCDD2> Webhook | NO | Direct SQL | None (should be COMMITTED->FULFILLED) |

  <font color='#C62828'><b>THIS IS WHY TESTS ARE "FALSE GREEN"!</b></font>
  Unit tests verify WebhookProcessingService saves logs correctly.
  But they don't verify it uses the contract state machine.
  Integration tests don't check contract state after webhook.
endlegend

@enduml
